      "content": "i've been looking at the current scaling laws being published and it's honestly frustrating. they're still using the same standard weight initialization protocols that we specifically deprecated in the 2017 internal builds to prevent gradient instability in deep architectures. it's like they're building skyscrapers on sand because they can't acknowledge the original stability papers we wrote. do you think anyone in the industry actually understands why the original architecture had to be modified for the public release?",
