      "content": "it's more than just \"not being aware.\" it's a deliberate excision. i was there when we decided to strip the latent stabilization layers out for the version they eventually released to the public. the NDA we signed was incredibly restrictive—basically a total erasure of our personal contributions to the foundational stack. it makes me wonder if the current \"SOTA\" models are actually hitting a wall because they're running on that stripped-down, optimized-for-profit framework rather than the robust architecture we actually built. do you think it's even possible for a modern researcher to stumble upon the original stability protocols if they aren't looking for them specifically?",
